      "data": {
        "text": "**Developing the Tool**\n\nI've completed the initial setup for the JSON extraction tool, crafting the `extract_json.py` file. I'm leveraging Google Cloud Vertex AI's `gemini-pro` model, initialized with `vertexai.init` and instantiated with `GenerativeModel(\"gemini-pro\")`. Placeholder comments are in place. Now I'll move on to testing and refining.\n\n\n**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI've got the `extract_json.py` file fully functional now. I've successfully implemented the JSON extraction functionality using the Gemini Pro model via Vertex AI, and it's all clearly defined via `vertexai.init` and `GenerativeModel(\"gemini-pro\")`. The user can provide their specific configurations such as `YOUR_PROJECT_ID` and `YOUR_REGION` via placeholder comments.\n\nI have incorporated the `extract_json_from_text` function, and it incorporates text and a prompt, crafting a detailed full prompt for the LLM. It then attempts a JSON parse of the LLM response. I also included example usage in the `if __name__ == '__main__':` block, so that the user can get started quickly.\n\n\n",
